+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the same JSON Schema that tools expose to providers, so malformed model calls can be corrected before an executor sees them.
+
+## Contract
+
+1. `execute` validates required properties, declared types and enum constraints before execution, returns a descriptive `ToolResponse` on rejection without invoking the executor, reports property paths and constraints without input values in results or logs, and passes accepted input (including unknown keys) unchanged exactly once without defaults or coercion; unknown tool names still throw `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#1: rejects invalid input safely and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L21))
+2. Static schemas compile at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and the compiled validator is reused across execution calls. ([validated by: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#2: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L76))
+3. Function-valued definitions resolve for each execution and validate against the current schema, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name. ([validated by: specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md#3: validates each dynamic schema and reuses its compiled validator](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L102))
+
+## Integration and delivery
+
+The rejection response uses the existing tool-result conversation path, allowing a corrected retry within the existing five-tool-round budget; validation itself does not throw for rejected input, while unknown tool names retain their existing exception contract.
+
+Delivery includes a runtime JSON Schema validator dependency, a one-line `execute` comment pointing here, updated README and tool-author guidance, updated `.specify/spec.md`, a consumer-facing changelog, a MINOR version bump, and a migration note explaining that executors no longer receive malformed inputs to hand-validate.
